89:We  tested  whether  normative  brain  regional  Z-scores have  an  advantage  over  the  observed  morphometric measures in predicting diagnostic status and symptom severity using psychosis as an example. For this test, we downloaded and parcellated (with FreeSurfer version 7 .1.0) T1 -weighted  images  from  the  repository  of  the  Human Connectome  Project-Early  Psychosis  Study  (HCP-EP). The HCP-EP cohort comprises 91 individuals with early psychosis and 57 healthy individuals (total sample 48 females and 100 males; age range 16·67-35·67 years). Sex (ie, male or female) was determined by self-report. 22 Each of the algorithms examined here were then applied to generate brain regional Z-scores in the HCP-EP cohort.
